0x413F94D0 — Lag-comp acceptability gate
----------------------------------------
Purpose: Returns al=1 (accept) or al=0 (reject) for whether a lag-comp record
   is still usable. Computes horizontal distance from record origin to current
   position and compares against max lag-comp distance [0x4206CDC0].
Confidence: OBSERVED (disassembly decoded from live memory).
Direct callers: 0x4148F441 (break_lagcomp_distance_a), 0x4148F7AB
   (break_lagcomp_distance_b).
Callees: none (leaf).
Key instructions (OBSERVED):
   0x413F94D5: mov edx,[0x4223F428]           ; context
   0x413F94DB: mov esi,[ecx+0x84]             ; record.tick
   0x413F94E1: mov al,1                       ; default accept
   0x413F94E3: cmp [edx+0x16C],esi            ; server_tick == record.tick ?
   0x413F94E9: je   0x413F9552                ; equal -> accept
   0x413F94EB: movsd xmm0,[ecx+0x18]          ; record origin x,y (packed)
   0x413F94F0: mulps xmm0,xmm0
   0x413F94F6: shufps xmm1,xmm0,0x55
   0x413F94FA: addss xmm1,xmm0
   0x413F94FE: xorps xmm0,xmm0
   0x413F9501: sqrtss xmm0,xmm1               ; horizontal distance
   0x413F9505: ucomiss xmm0,[0x4206CDC0]      ; max lag-comp distance (=100.0)
   0x413F950C: jbe  0x413F9552                ; within limit -> accept
   0x413F950E: ...                            ; reject path, computes scaled value
Record origin x,y stored at record+0x18. Horizontal distance only.
Note: overwriting the call at 0x4148F441 with "mov al,0;nop;nop;nop" forces
al=0 => always reject. UI label "Remove Useless Lag Comp. delay" is inverted
relative to what the patch does (verified mechanism).
---- Pseudocode (reconstructed) ----
bool lagcomp_acceptable(record* r) {
    ctx = *(uint32_t*)0x4223F428;
    if (*(uint32_t*)(ctx + 0x16C) == r->tick) return true;
    float dx = r->origin_x - cur_x;   // actually [ecx+0x18] packed x,y
    float dy = r->origin_y - cur_y;
    float dist = sqrtf(dx*dx + dy*dy);
    if (dist <= *(float*)0x4206CDC0) return true;   // 100.0f
    ... scaled rejection computation ...
    return false;   // al ends as 0 on reject path
}

